    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 3 tests pass with a clean build. The implementation is complete and green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added an optional `postcode` field to the owner, validated only when present, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions.\n\n**Contract & persistence**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added `postcode` to the `OwnerFields` schema (4-digit string; `Owner` inherits it via `allOf`, so it's stored and returned). Not in `required`, keeping the request backward-compatible.\n- `Owner.java` \u2014 added the `postcode` column + getter/setter.\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` \u2014 added the `postcode` column to the `owners` table.\n- MapStruct's `OwnerMapper` maps `postcode` by name automatically (both directions), so no mapper change was needed.\n\n**Validation (when present)**\n- `Localities.postcodeRange(region)` \u2014 added the fixed region\u2192range table (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099); returns `null` for unknown regions.\n- `OwnerPostcode` (new helper) \u2014 no-op when absent/blank; else requires exactly 4 digits and, for a city with a known region, enforces the range. Unknown-region cities accept any 4-digit postcode.\n- Wired into `ValidateOwnerFields` (POST) and `ValidateOwner` (PUT); `ApplyOwner` now copies `postcode` on update.\n\n**Error handling (400)**\n- New checked `InvalidOwnerPostcodeException`, its `InvalidOwnerPostcodeExceptionHandler` (responds 400 with `{\"errors\":[\"postcode\"]}`), and the escalation YAML mapping the exception to the handler \u2014 matching the existing email/telephone pattern.\n\nThe three acceptance tests (`coreStoresValidPostcode`, `coreAcceptsOwnerWithoutPostcode`, `errorRejectsMalformedPostcode`) all pass, and the full suite is green.",
